---
import InfoLayout from '../layouts/InfoLayout.astro';
import { projects, projectUrl } from '../data/projects';
---
<InfoLayout
  path="/about"
  title="About RateKit"
  description="RateKit is a collection of free business calculators for founders, freelancers and entrepreneurs. No signup, no data stored."
  pageTag="About us"
  h1="About RateKit"
  pageSub="Free, fast, and honest business calculators. No fluff, no upsells, no data harvesting."
  breadcrumbLabel="About"
>
  <div class="highlight-box">
    <strong>Our mission:</strong> Give every founder, freelancer, and entrepreneur instant access to professional-grade financial calculators — completely free, no signup required.
  </div>

  <h2>Why RateKit Exists</h2>
  <p>Too many financial tools are either buried behind paywalls, require account creation just to see a number, or are cluttered with ads and dark patterns. We built RateKit because we believe the basic math of running a business should be accessible to everyone.</p>
  <p>Every calculator on RateKit works instantly in your browser. No data is sent to our servers. No account needed. No credit card. Just the numbers you need.</p>

  <h2>What We Build</h2>
  <p>RateKit focuses on practical tools for two main audiences:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Freelancers & Consultants</strong> — Freelance rate calculator, Stripe/PayPal fee calculator, Self-employment tax estimator, VAT/GST calculator</li>
    <li><strong>Founders & Startups</strong> — SAFE equity calculator, Burn rate & runway, LTV:CAC ratio, Break-even analysis, ROI calculator, Business loan calculator</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Our Principles</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>✅ Always free for core features</li>
    <li>✅ No account required to use calculators</li>
    <li>✅ Your data stays in your browser</li>
    <li>✅ No dark patterns or misleading results</li>
    <li>✅ Formulas based on publicly accepted financial standards</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Coming Soon</h2>
  <p>We are working on optional user accounts that will let you save and revisit your calculations. This will always be free for core features. Premium features (branded PDF exports, unlimited saved calculations) may be available for a small fee in the future.</p>

  <h2>Who's Behind RateKit</h2>
  <p>RateKit is built and maintained by <strong>Azat Israilov</strong>. You can see my other work at <a href="https://azatisrail.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener">azatisrail.org</a>.</p>
  <p>I'm open to suggestions, bug reports, and ideas for what to build next — email me directly at <a href="mailto:connect4fund@gmail.com">connect4fund@gmail.com</a>.</p>

  <h2>Our Projects</h2>
  <p>RateKit is one of several sites built by the same team. Each is available in English and Russian:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>RateKit</strong> (this site) — business calculators for founders and business owners, and now much more.</li>
    {projects.map((p) => (
      <li><a href={projectUrl(p.url, 'about')} target="_blank" rel="noopener">{p.name}</a> — {p.en}</li>
    ))}
  </ul>

  <h2>Contact Us</h2>
  <p>Have a suggestion for a new calculator? Found a bug? Just want to say hi?</p>
  <p>Email us at <a href="mailto:connect4fund@gmail.com">connect4fund@gmail.com</a> or visit our <a href="/contact">contact page</a>.</p>

  <h2>☕ Buy Me a Coffee</h2>
  <p>RateKit runs on free coffee and the mild delusion that these calculators actually help people. If one of them just saved you from a spreadsheet disaster, you could buy me an actual coffee — or don't, no popups, no guilt trip, I promise. <a href="https://ko-fi.com/ontoguzlabs" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Ko-fi</a> · <a href="https://patreon.com/AzatIsrailov" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Patreon</a>.</p>
</InfoLayout>
